WEBVTT

01:33.980 --> 01:35.990
Caution: Children at Play

01:35.990 --> 01:38.490
Cafe Tet-chan

01:37.180 --> 01:38.490
Intense!

01:38.820 --> 01:41.740
You looked so intense, manager!
Even at that age!

01:41.740 --> 01:44.380
You don't look like a high
school student at all.

01:44.380 --> 01:46.500
You look more like an old man
in a boys' school uniform!

01:46.500 --> 01:48.680
The only difference is the glasses.

01:48.680 --> 01:50.320
How many years were you held back?

01:50.320 --> 01:51.500
I was never held back!

01:51.830 --> 01:57.510
You mock your senpai's youth now,
but you'll be old men too, soon enough.

01:55.980 --> 01:57.510
Cafe Tet-chan Proprietor
Asahina Tetsu

01:58.460 --> 01:59.760
Our omelet katsu rice is here!

02:00.110 --> 02:01.260
Here you go!

02:02.350 --> 02:03.260
It looks great!

02:03.870 --> 02:05.770
Let's eat!

02:06.140 --> 02:09.770
The fun times always seem
to end in an instant.

02:09.770 --> 02:13.770
At the same time, your boring
classes seem to go on forever.

02:13.770 --> 02:15.620
That's right!

02:15.620 --> 02:19.530
Anyway, who was it that decided
there should be 60 minutes in an hour?

02:19.890 --> 02:22.030
It's been that way since forever.

02:22.030 --> 02:25.730
But what if there were
55 minutes in an hour?

02:25.730 --> 02:27.620
Then we'd get out of
class that much sooner

02:27.620 --> 02:29.420
and get to start club
that much sooner, right?

02:29.420 --> 02:33.320
Yes! Such out-of-the-box
thinking is very important!

02:34.040 --> 02:35.050
Right!

02:36.800 --> 02:39.050
Hayato got praised by Soma-senpai?

02:39.050 --> 02:44.560
But he's never praised me before...

02:39.430 --> 02:43.850
But he's never praised me
before... before... before...

02:44.930 --> 02:45.810
Glasses
Club

02:49.130 --> 02:52.750
Yukiya! I want you to produce a large
number of these 55-minute clocks, ASAP!

02:52.750 --> 02:53.690
Understood.

02:54.440 --> 02:57.190
Let's get our boring classes
over as soon as possible!

02:58.490 --> 03:01.490
We'll have the news from
Fukui Shimbun at 6 o'clock.

03:04.990 --> 03:10.000
I Hope You Finish the X-Ray Glasses

03:26.730 --> 03:28.420
Want to get a quick drink?

03:28.420 --> 03:30.730
That sounds good. I'll join you.

03:35.360 --> 03:37.480
This is Purple Under-Rim.

03:37.480 --> 03:39.990
Black Square, please respond.

03:40.410 --> 03:42.320
This is Black Square.

03:42.650 --> 03:44.950
The last two have gone home.

03:44.950 --> 03:47.390
The school should now be empty.

03:47.390 --> 03:48.080
Roger.

03:49.290 --> 03:50.250
Let's go!

03:50.250 --> 03:54.120
"Operation: Starting Tomorrow There
Will Be 55 Minutes in an Hour," begin!

03:55.290 --> 03:56.880
Fifty-five!

03:56.880 --> 03:58.590
One hour!

03:58.590 --> 04:00.340
One hour!

04:02.220 --> 04:05.780
Ready? Yukiya, Hayato and I will
cover the 3rd and 4th floors!

04:05.760 --> 04:07.550
Takuma and Mitsuki, cover
the 1st and 2nd floors!

04:07.550 --> 04:08.750
And also the gym!

04:08.750 --> 04:09.720
Roger!

04:10.140 --> 04:13.480
Why does Hayato get to
be with Soma-senpai?

04:34.290 --> 04:36.790
Broadcasting Room

04:35.180 --> 04:36.790
Okay, this is the last one.

04:38.980 --> 04:39.700
Here.

04:41.750 --> 04:42.580
Huh?

04:42.580 --> 04:43.800
What is it?

04:43.800 --> 04:46.570
What is this? A hidden door?

04:48.530 --> 04:49.790
There's something here.

04:56.230 --> 04:58.310
A glasses case?

04:58.810 --> 05:00.070
A glasses case?

05:03.360 --> 05:06.610
They're sunglasses! Really old ones!

05:06.990 --> 05:08.120
Those are...

05:09.950 --> 05:10.950
There's no question!

05:11.330 --> 05:14.750
They're the Ray-Ban teardrop gold frames

05:14.750 --> 05:17.000
that the Boss wore in that
old national police drama!

05:16.990 --> 05:19.710
They're discontinued, which
makes them super-rare now!

05:19.710 --> 05:23.140
It's awful to see them
reduced to this state!

05:23.140 --> 05:24.630
We have to repair them immediately.

05:24.630 --> 05:26.250
Yukiya, take care of it.

05:26.250 --> 05:27.740
Okay. Understood.

05:29.630 --> 05:31.720
How did things go? Did you finish?

05:31.720 --> 05:35.770
Yes! We successfully replaced all
the clocks with 55-minute clocks!

05:36.230 --> 05:39.020
Yes! Mission comple—

05:38.040 --> 05:39.770
Hey, Soma-kun.

05:40.580 --> 05:42.020
What do we do about that?

05:42.360 --> 05:43.120
Huh?

05:50.780 --> 05:52.930
I didn't think that far.

06:01.790 --> 06:03.170
Good morning!

06:04.300 --> 06:06.800
Normal
Echizen-Takefu

06:10.300 --> 06:13.510
And from that, we can
conclude that x equals...

06:16.730 --> 06:20.520
It's over already? It seems like time
is passing very quickly today.

06:24.530 --> 06:26.190
<i>It's a big success, huh?</i>

06:26.190 --> 06:28.780
<i>No one's caught on!</i>

06:28.780 --> 06:29.820
Stand!

06:29.820 --> 06:31.780
<i>The 55-minute clocks
are operating properly.</i>

06:31.780 --> 06:32.740
Bow!

06:33.330 --> 06:36.040
<i>It's a good thing the
big clock stopped.</i>

06:40.370 --> 06:42.790
<i>Let's keep this up and have
an abridged 2nd period, too!</i>

06:47.450 --> 06:50.380
Okay! That's all for today's class.

06:50.380 --> 06:52.010
Faculty Office

06:54.240 --> 06:55.650
What's wrong, Kyosuke?

06:55.650 --> 06:59.730
I just bought this watch,
but it's already running slow.

06:59.730 --> 07:01.460
What? Yours, too?

07:01.460 --> 07:02.020
Huh?

07:02.020 --> 07:04.580
Well, my watch is running slow, too.

07:04.580 --> 07:06.780
Mine's pretty old, though.

07:06.780 --> 07:09.400
Um, my watch is running slow, too!

07:09.400 --> 07:10.570
My watch, too!

07:10.570 --> 07:12.280
The clock on my cell phone, too!

07:12.660 --> 07:14.160
See?

07:14.160 --> 07:16.240
They're all showing the same time.

07:16.240 --> 07:18.910
Which means... You don't think...

07:21.960 --> 07:25.830
Listen. Before we start class,
there's something I'd like to make clear.

07:25.830 --> 07:29.170
We've found that, for some reason,
all the clocks in the school are wrong.

07:29.170 --> 07:33.430
That's why we're going to
run 3rd period by my watch.

07:34.700 --> 07:35.870
Looks like they caught on.

07:35.870 --> 07:37.430
Looks like.

07:37.430 --> 07:38.430
Glasses!

07:38.430 --> 07:40.310
Glasses

07:40.770 --> 07:43.550
So the plan was a failure
in the end, huh?

07:43.550 --> 07:46.820
We worked quickly, but they
caught on quickly, too.

07:46.820 --> 07:48.820
But it wasn't in vain.

07:49.820 --> 07:51.820
What do you mean?

07:51.820 --> 07:54.820
Constructing those 55-minute
clocks gave me a hint

07:54.810 --> 07:57.330
for how to approach
the X-Ray Glasses.

07:57.730 --> 08:00.200
If I do it this way, I think it will work.

08:00.710 --> 08:01.580
Really?

08:09.560 --> 08:13.830
It's done. The X-Ray Glasses
Mk. 35 are complete.

08:13.830 --> 08:16.850
X-Ray Glasses Mk. 35

08:16.850 --> 08:19.770
These are the X-Ray Glasses Mk. 35?

08:19.770 --> 08:23.520
I've really got a feeling about these.
To be honest, I'm proud of the result.

08:24.080 --> 08:28.270
These definitely seem a cut
above the earlier X-Ray Glasses!

08:28.270 --> 08:31.030
As club president, you should
be the first to wear them.

08:31.360 --> 08:32.280
Yeah.

08:32.280 --> 08:34.660
But we're all men here.

08:34.660 --> 08:38.530
Let's go out into town and
find a pretty lady, quick!

08:38.910 --> 08:40.290
No! I cannot wait!

08:40.290 --> 08:44.790
I must know the capabilities of the
X-Ray Glasses Mk. 35 right this moment!

08:46.290 --> 08:48.540
At this stage, even a man will do!

08:48.540 --> 08:51.290
W-Wait! Not me!

08:53.380 --> 08:57.800
<i>At this stage, even a man...
even a man... even a man...</i>

08:57.800 --> 08:59.550
You can use me!

09:02.840 --> 09:03.740
Mitsuki...

09:14.850 --> 09:16.320
Are you sure?

09:17.850 --> 09:18.820
Yes!

09:19.290 --> 09:20.830
Okay! I'm going to look!

09:21.340 --> 09:22.830
Please do!

09:32.250 --> 09:36.840
<i>Ah... Soma-senpai can see all of me.</i>

09:40.550 --> 09:44.350
<i>He's looking at me!
Soma-senpai's gaze feels so hot.</i>

09:50.810 --> 09:52.480
They're not X-ray at all.

09:55.150 --> 09:56.360
A failure?

09:57.310 --> 09:59.030
A failure?

09:59.450 --> 10:01.490
Well, don't get too down, Yukiya!

10:01.490 --> 10:05.540
We can start on the X-Ray
Glasses Mk. 36 right away and...

10:10.420 --> 10:12.880
Who are you?

10:27.100 --> 10:29.440
What year are you in? What class?

10:29.440 --> 10:31.270
And how long have you been here?

10:31.270 --> 10:33.570
You can't just enter the
club room without asking!

10:37.740 --> 10:40.860
Hold on. Who are you talking to?

10:40.860 --> 10:43.660
Who? Who are you?

10:43.660 --> 10:46.290
I'm Mochizuki Koichi.

10:44.620 --> 10:46.290
Mochizuki Koichi

10:46.790 --> 10:48.870
Mochizuki Koichi, he says.

10:51.130 --> 10:54.590
Wh-What's going on, Soma-senpai?

10:54.590 --> 10:58.590
Did you eat a rotten cream puff and
start hallucinating or something?

10:58.590 --> 10:59.630
I wonder...

11:00.010 --> 11:03.180
Akira, take off the X-Ray Glasses.

11:03.930 --> 11:05.140
Sure.

11:06.390 --> 11:07.390
Huh?

11:11.270 --> 11:12.940
When I put them on, I can see him.

11:12.940 --> 11:14.730
When I take them off,
I can't see him.

11:14.730 --> 11:23.120
See him, can't see him.
See him, can't see him.

11:29.620 --> 11:33.130
You don't think these are
glasses that can see ghosts?

11:34.380 --> 11:38.590
It appears that instead of creating
glasses that see through,

11:35.340 --> 11:42.180
Glasses That See Through

11:38.590 --> 11:41.800
I accidentally created
glasses that see ghosts.

11:39.470 --> 11:42.180
Glasses That See Ghosts

11:44.850 --> 11:49.390
Ghosts

11:46.390 --> 11:49.390
Through

11:46.470 --> 11:49.390
It's amazing what a difference
one word can make!

11:49.390 --> 11:52.730
Even Minabe-kun's failures
are successes, after all.

11:52.730 --> 11:55.110
Which means the "feeling"
I had when I finished them

11:55.110 --> 11:57.360
was the feeling that I'd
made spirit-seeing glasses?

11:58.860 --> 12:00.400
I can see him!

12:00.400 --> 12:02.660
I can see ghosts without
even wearing the glasses!

12:02.660 --> 12:05.410
Why can I see ghosts? Why?!

12:10.410 --> 12:14.420
So what is a ghost like you
doing in our club room?

12:14.920 --> 12:17.420
You guys pulled me out.

12:17.750 --> 12:18.670
Huh?

12:18.670 --> 12:22.540
You took the sunglasses out of the hidden
compartment in the broadcast room, right?

12:22.540 --> 12:24.640
Oh, the sunglasses!

12:24.640 --> 12:26.430
I was dwelling in them.

12:27.160 --> 12:29.310
Does that mean you're...

12:31.890 --> 12:33.310
...a sunglasses fairy?!

12:33.310 --> 12:34.350
No!

12:34.940 --> 12:36.150
Question!

12:36.150 --> 12:37.110
Yes?

12:37.110 --> 12:40.730
How come I'm the only one who can
see you without the glasses on?

12:40.730 --> 12:44.320
That's probably because you were
the first one to touch the sunglasses.

12:45.320 --> 12:47.870
I'm not sure if that answers
my question or not...

12:47.870 --> 12:52.200
By the way, there's a favor
I'd like to ask of you guys.

12:52.200 --> 12:53.710
A favor?

12:54.580 --> 12:56.960
Would you let me join the Glasses Club?

12:58.590 --> 13:01.560
We can't let a ghost join the club!

13:01.560 --> 13:02.820
Even I'm just a—

13:01.980 --> 13:02.820
Yes!

13:02.820 --> 13:06.640
Even if you are a ghost, no one
who wears glasses can be bad!

13:06.640 --> 13:11.140
Therefore, I accept Mochizuki Koichi
into the club as a special member!

13:13.060 --> 13:16.190
I'm Hachimine Takuma, a second year.
Pleased to meet you.

13:17.940 --> 13:18.690
This way.

13:20.190 --> 13:21.690
I'm Kamatani Mitsuki.

13:22.070 --> 13:23.690
Minabe Yukiya.

13:27.950 --> 13:32.700
Not dead, but a provisional member

13:28.450 --> 13:32.700
Even I'm just a provisional
member, and I'm not dead...

13:32.700 --> 13:33.700
Glasses!

13:34.710 --> 13:35.710
I'm back!

13:36.170 --> 13:37.210
Welcome back!

13:38.790 --> 13:40.340
What? A visitor?

13:40.790 --> 13:41.340
Huh?

13:41.960 --> 13:45.050
Oh, I thought someone was with you.

13:45.630 --> 13:47.300
Probably just your imagination.

13:57.900 --> 13:58.810
I came along!

13:58.810 --> 14:00.270
Why?

14:00.270 --> 14:02.440
Well, I didn't have anywhere else to go.

14:02.440 --> 14:04.610
Why don't you just stay at the school?

14:04.610 --> 14:06.990
And anyway, now that you're free,

14:06.990 --> 14:09.570
why don't you just
rest in peace already?

14:13.830 --> 14:15.620
Sob sob sob...

14:15.620 --> 14:17.410
That's so mean, Akira-kun,

14:16.580 --> 14:21.420
Hold on, having a ghost whining
on me is no laughing matter.

14:17.410 --> 14:21.420
saying that to me after you let
me into the Glasses Club.

14:21.420 --> 14:23.090
Then I can stay?

14:24.000 --> 14:26.470
Yes, but just for tonight.

14:30.010 --> 14:31.470
But even so...

14:33.310 --> 14:35.720
I didn't say you could
take a bath with me!

14:36.060 --> 14:38.390
It's okay! We're both guys, anyway.

14:39.980 --> 14:40.730
It's <i>not</i> okay!

14:52.570 --> 14:53.780
So heavy...

14:58.660 --> 15:00.620
Sorry, did I wake you?

15:00.620 --> 15:02.670
"Did I wake you?"
What do you think?!

15:03.130 --> 15:06.090
That's it! You're outta here!

15:06.090 --> 15:08.550
Get out of my house, now!

15:12.300 --> 15:14.260
Okay! I'm sorry!

15:14.260 --> 15:16.720
I'm sorry, so stop summoning
flames so close to your glasses!

15:16.720 --> 15:18.310
It's gonna warp the frames!

15:19.020 --> 15:22.060
But even so, I didn't say
you could sleep next to me.

15:25.650 --> 15:27.440
About what I said before...

15:29.990 --> 15:32.950
Is there some reason you
can't rest in peace?

15:43.500 --> 15:46.960
It was the summer of my
second year of high school.

15:49.920 --> 15:52.430
Normal
Takefushin

15:53.510 --> 15:58.680
I accidentally broke a pair of sunglasses
I borrowed from a good friend in my class.

15:58.680 --> 16:01.190
You mean those Ray-Bans.

16:01.190 --> 16:06.690
Yeah, but I couldn't admit it to him.

16:07.980 --> 16:11.900
I was in the Broadcasting Club, so I
hid the broken sunglasses in a cupboard,

16:11.900 --> 16:15.490
then lied to my friend saying
I'd already returned them.

16:17.370 --> 16:19.910
And you had a fight about it, right?

16:19.910 --> 16:21.080
Yeah.

16:21.080 --> 16:23.790
Of course, the whole argument was
just, "I already returned them."

16:23.790 --> 16:25.080
"No you didn't."

16:29.590 --> 16:34.390
But on the way home, I started
realizing that I'd done something terrible.

16:34.390 --> 16:38.260
I decided I would apologize to him
about the sunglasses, and turned around.

16:39.100 --> 16:40.270
And just then...

16:47.560 --> 16:49.780
<i>I have to return those sunglasses!</i>

16:50.690 --> 16:52.780
But just before I died,

16:52.780 --> 16:55.660
my soul cried out with those words,

16:55.660 --> 16:57.830
and I flew back to the school.

16:57.830 --> 17:01.000
I came to dwell in the sunglasses.

17:06.790 --> 17:07.920
In other words,

17:07.920 --> 17:11.620
you regretted the fact that
you died before returning

17:11.620 --> 17:15.010
the broken sunglasses to your friend,
so you can't rest in peace?

17:15.630 --> 17:18.260
It must have been divine retribution.

17:18.260 --> 17:22.140
Now that I'm dead, I can't
repair and return the glasses,

17:23.600 --> 17:25.890
or see him and apologize.

17:27.900 --> 17:31.530
But when I saw you all
having so much fun...

17:38.320 --> 17:41.660
I realized that I don't want to
leave things at that fight.

17:41.660 --> 17:43.950
I want to apologize properly for

17:43.950 --> 17:47.670
breaking the sunglasses,
and for lying to him.

17:50.340 --> 17:51.800
Sunglasses, huh?

17:53.550 --> 17:57.180
I feel like I've seen that
face somewhere before.

18:00.600 --> 18:03.640
That friend of yours.
Was his name...

18:08.560 --> 18:10.560
Closed
Cafe Tet-chan

18:10.560 --> 18:12.570
Cafe Tet-chan

18:12.950 --> 18:14.320
Mornin'!

18:14.320 --> 18:17.070
We aren't open for business yet.

18:17.560 --> 18:20.700
Actually, there was someone
I wanted you to see.

18:21.170 --> 18:22.580
Shirogane-sensei!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.790
Oh, Kyosuke. You're here early.

18:24.790 --> 18:26.640
Look at this!

18:26.640 --> 18:28.830
I found them hidden behind
the gym storehouse!

18:30.930 --> 18:33.910
When the hell did this happen?

18:35.620 --> 18:37.340
Someone you want me to see?

18:37.340 --> 18:40.090
But there's no one here but you.

18:40.540 --> 18:42.720
Just try putting these on.

18:42.720 --> 18:43.600
What?

18:52.870 --> 18:54.050
Tet-chan!

18:55.130 --> 18:56.110
You're...

18:57.900 --> 18:59.880
Koichi, aren't you?

18:59.880 --> 19:02.240
It's been a long time, Tet-chan.

19:02.870 --> 19:05.620
You look just like you did then!

19:08.210 --> 19:11.380
No, you look just
like you did then, too.

19:11.850 --> 19:15.020
There's something I
have to return to you.

19:17.970 --> 19:19.880
These are my...

19:19.880 --> 19:22.640
I lied when I said I'd
already returned them.

19:23.310 --> 19:25.040
The truth is, I broke them.

19:26.230 --> 19:29.890
I'm sorry that I lied.

19:37.990 --> 19:40.650
It took me thirty years to fix them.

19:41.530 --> 19:44.180
Wow, they're not prescription,
and they're so dark!

19:44.180 --> 19:45.370
I can't see.

19:45.370 --> 19:47.530
I envy people with good eyesight.

19:47.530 --> 19:50.660
Prescription sunglasses are too
expensive for me to afford them.

19:50.660 --> 19:52.860
Some day when we can afford them,

19:52.860 --> 19:54.920
let's put them on and
play around together.

20:11.850 --> 20:14.480
Yeah, I still can't see a thing!

20:15.730 --> 20:18.280
You probably can't see
because you're cry—

20:18.730 --> 20:21.280
I can't see either! I can't see!

20:23.950 --> 20:25.370
This is the last one.

20:29.910 --> 20:34.120
Time is returning to normal.
I have to go, too.

20:35.210 --> 20:36.170
You're going?

20:36.880 --> 20:37.920
Yeah.

20:38.840 --> 20:41.130
Goodbye! Take care in the next world!

20:42.260 --> 20:43.510
This way!

20:43.930 --> 20:46.510
Thank you, everyone. Goodbye.

20:46.510 --> 20:47.760
Bye.

20:47.760 --> 20:48.850
Be well!

20:48.850 --> 20:49.770
Goodbye!

20:50.520 --> 20:52.060
Tet-chan, goodbye.

20:52.060 --> 20:55.060
Prescription sunglasses!

20:55.850 --> 20:58.690
I'll buy a pair for each of us,
and bring them with me.

21:06.370 --> 21:08.700
Just take your time, okay?

21:10.290 --> 21:14.460
I hope you finish the X-Ray Glasses!

21:14.460 --> 21:15.960
I'll do my best!

21:18.630 --> 21:20.460
Just watch me, Senpai!

21:24.430 --> 21:26.470
By the way, we're late to class.

21:26.470 --> 21:28.970
Oh no! Hurry, everyone!

23:11.870 --> 23:13.950
Nose pads sit between the glasses

23:12.120 --> 23:20.710
Nose Pads

23:13.450 --> 23:15.160
Glasses

23:13.950 --> 23:16.000
and the bridge of the nose,
acting as a cushion.

23:15.160 --> 23:16.660
Glasses
Cushion

23:16.000 --> 23:18.750
They're important components
that hold the glasses in place.

23:16.660 --> 23:20.710
Glasses
Cushion
Hold in Place

23:17.710 --> 23:20.710
Important Components

23:18.750 --> 23:24.340
A true glasses wearer must <i>never</i>
refer to them as "those nose things."

23:20.750 --> 23:21.330
NEVER!!

